\title{gllvmTMB: Generalised Linear Latent Variable Models with TMB}
\description{
\if{html}{\figure{logo.png}{options: style='float: right' alt='logo' width='120'}}

Fits multivariate models for data where each site, individual, species, or study has several responses. Start from a wide data frame with the 'traits()' formula interface, or from already-stacked long data, and estimate trait covariance, pairwise correlations, shared latent axes, and trait-specific variance. Binary presence-absence applications include binomial-family joint species distribution models. Optional animal, phylogenetic, spatial, and known-sampling-variance components use the same formula grammar. Model fitting uses Template Model Builder (Kristensen et al. 2016 \doi{10.18637/jss.v070.i05}). This experimental package should be used through its documented tutorials and model-specific boundaries; convergence alone does not establish that an estimate or interval is reliable. Broad package-wide interval coverage is not yet confirmed. A handful of standardized-loading interval calculations have been checked for one Gaussian model, in a few fixed sample-size and rank combinations, and for one fixed simulated dataset with known true values. They are only for fits that converge cleanly. They do not carry over to other sample sizes, ranks, models, or datasets. Total-variance penalty profiles remain approximate; agreement with the exact answer has not been confirmed.
}
